ics compatibility&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#8e24aa;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="935" y="1030" width="720" height="100" /></mxCell><mxCell id="e_fused_cl5" parent="1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#8e24aa;dashed=1;" edge="1" source="fused" target="cl5"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cl6" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;AUT — Autonomous Operations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:10px;'&gt;mission manager · C2 · contingency · remote supervision&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#8e24aa;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1735" y="1030" width="720" height="100" /></mxCell><mxCell id="e_fused_cl6" parent="1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#8e24aa;dashed=1;" edge="1" source="fused" target="cl6"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cl7" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;SAF — Safety / V&amp;V&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:10px;'&gt;H2 hazards · HV isolation · fire detection · fault containment&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#8e24aa;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2535" y="1030" width="720" height="100" /></mxCell><mxCell id="e_fused_cl7" parent="1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#8e24aa;dashed=1;" edge="1" source="fused" target="cl7"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="n8" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;Source-status note:&lt;/b&gt; the cited partnership page is a 2023 announcement. Statements there about prototype maturity and then-target certification dates are historical claims and are not used here as current certification status. The architecture only derives stable requirement themes: BWB cargo volume, hydrogen storage integration, fuel-cell electric propulsion, autonomy, and cargo/logistics compatibility." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="130" y="1450" width="3190" height="100" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="5cadc6a7" name="09_Hydrogen_Electric_Reqs"><mxGraphModel dx="2500" dy="1800" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="3600" pageHeight="2700" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" parent="1" value="Hydrogen-Electric Propulsion — High-Level Technical Requirements&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:11px;'&gt;System-level requirement decomposition for research and simulation. Exact pressures, tank geometry, cell chemistry, voltages and thermal limits remain TBD and require qualified detailed engineering.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="20" width="3440" height="78" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g1" parent="1" value="H2S-100 — Hydrogen Storage" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e3f2fd;strokeColor=#1976d2;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=8;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="70" y="150" width="800" height="660" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g1_0" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;H2S-101&lt;/b&gt; Mission hydrogen capacity&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:9px;'&gt;Target: TBD&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fill